{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 32, "model_name": "abacusai/dracarys-llama-3.1-70b-instruct", "content": "the social network is a film that tells the story of the founding of facebook and the subsequent lawsuits that followed. the movie is directed by david fincher and written by aaron sorkin. the film stars jesse eisenberg as mark zuckerberg, andrew garfield as eduardo saverin, and justin timberlake as sean parker.\n\nthe movie begins with mark zuckerberg, a sophomore at harvard university, creating a website called \"facemash\" that allows users to compare the photos of two students and vote on which one is more attractive. the site becomes a huge success, but also generates a lot of controversy and gets zuckerberg in trouble with the university.\n\nafter the success of facemash, zuckerberg is approached by cameron and tyler winklevoss, two harvard students who want him to help them create a social networking site for the university. zuckerberg agrees to help them, but eventually drops the project and creates his own site, thefacebook, with the help of his roommate eduardo saverin.\n\nthefacebook quickly becomes popular, and zuckerberg and saverin start to make money from the site. however, the winklevoss twins claim that zuckerberg stole their idea and sue him for intellectual property theft. the movie then follows the subsequent lawsuits and the rise of facebook to become one of the most popular social networking sites in the world.\n\nthe social network features a talented cast, with jesse eisenberg delivering a standout performance as mark zuckerberg. andrew garfield is also excellent as eduardo saverin, and justin timberlake is surprisingly good as sean parker, the co-founder of napster.\n\nthe film's direction by david fincher is also noteworthy. fincher's use of dark and muted colors creates a sense of unease and tension, which is fitting for a movie that deals with themes of betrayal and greed. the cinematography is also excellent,